    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [80, 580],
      "size": [850, 410],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "PLANAR HOLE PATCH QUICKSTART\n\n1. The bundled example.png is selected so the workflow validates on a clean install. Choose your plate in Load Image.\n2. Queue once. Atlas Derive Relief Mesh outputs its literal topology-hole mask.\n3. Atlas Planar Hole Patch rejects frame/oversize regions first, then attempts eligible islands smallest-first so sky gaps cannot consume the fit budget.\n4. Accepted vertices are camera-ray/plane intersections with exact projective UVs and shared perimeter indices.\n5. In Atlas Viewport enable Project and orbit gently. The remaining_holes output is wired to debug_matte; enable Matte to inspect what still needs a clean plate or a tighter artist mask.\n\nThe direct hole-mask wire is automatic mode. For deliberate silhouette repair, intersect it with a painted MASK before Atlas Planar Hole Patch."
      ],
      "color": "#25405c",
      "bgcolor": "#16283b"
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [1590, 500],
      "size": [520, 490],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 11,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "WHY THESE PATCH DEFAULTS\n\n• ring_cells = 3: enough surrounding relief to stabilize the angle.\n• max_components = 128: attempt every eligible island in an ordinary relief mesh; unsafe frame/oversize regions do not consume this budget.\n• normal_tolerance = 22°: defines which surrounding normals agree for each island.\n• min_normal_support = 0.30: the agreeing cluster must represent at least 30% of valid surrounding normals, allowing one-sided facade evidence.\n• The agreeing normals are averaged directly into the patch angle. max_plane_error = 0.20 m chooses/checks the densest local plane position when that angle appears at multiple depths.\n• max_hole_fraction = 4% and enclosed_only = true retain the sky/frame safety gates.\n\nThe report names the failed gate and measured agreement/residual. Geometry cannot invent hidden pixels; true disocclusion also needs a clean plate."
      ],
      "color": "#3b3156",
      "bgcolor": "#251d39"
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [2140, 500],
      "size": [850, 490],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 12,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "RETOPO + OPTIONAL WALL MERGE\n\nAtlas Retopologize Layer runs AFTER the planar patch, so the original relief and accepted planar patches are one mesh for decimation and UV regeneration. Decimate needs trimesh + fast-simplification; missing dependencies degrade softly and leave the patched solve unchanged.\n\nThe default viewport wire now comes DIRECTLY from Retopologize Layer so wall proxies cannot hide the patch result. The wall/merge branch remains as an optional disconnected experiment: max_objects = 0 prevents boxes/cubes, but Atlas Merge Geometry only appends wall primitives—it is not a boolean/weld and retopology does not fuse them."
      ],
      "color": "#4b3a24",
      "bgcolor": "#2e2215"
    }
